+## The formal proof and the elementary alternative
+
+This preserved formalization uses continuous functional calculus. Functional
+calculus is not mathematically necessary for the theorem: Section 4 of the
+corrected manuscript gives a paper-level dyadic proof using self-adjointness,
+Cauchy--Schwarz and the common exponential orbit rate. That elementary proof
+is not formalized in this module; its declarations below remain unchanged.
+
+Banach--Steinhaus cannot be applied directly to an arbitrary dense subspace.
+Strong convergence of powers of a norm-one positive contraction to zero also
+does not by itself give a uniform exponential rate. Those observations do not
+rule out the dyadic argument, which uses the stronger common-rate hypothesis.
+The earlier source commentary claiming necessity of functional calculus and
+insufficiency of powers is superseded by this correction.
 
